.TH RESOLVER 3
.SH NAME
res_init, res_mkquery, res_send, res_query, res_search, res_querydomain \- DNS stub resolver
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include <resolv.h>
.SH DESCRIPTION
res_init reads resolver(5). res_mkquery constructs a bounded DNS query with
an unpredictable ID. res_send returns a matching server reply into the
caller buffer; res_query also maps DNS errors into h_errno. res_search tries
the Lite2 domain search list and HOSTALIASES; res_querydomain joins a name
and domain or removes a final dot. Functions return the reply length or -1.
.PP
UDP uses SO_RCVTIMEO and retrans shifted by the attempt, divided by server
count after the first attempt. Replies must match source, port, ID, opcode
and question. Truncation retries over a length-prefixed TCP connection.
Oversized TCP replies are drained, returned clipped and marked truncated.
ECONNRESET allows one reconnect/requery. RES_USEVC forces TCP;
RES_STAYOPEN keeps a TCP connection until _res_close or an error.
.PP
EINTR stops immediately. A server refusal at every attempted server produces
ECONNREFUSED; a silent server does not. NXDOMAIN maps HOST_NOT_FOUND,
empty answers NO_DATA, SERVFAIL TRY_AGAIN, and permanent errors NO_RECOVERY.
SERVFAIL, NOTIMP and REFUSED skip a server. State and result storage are not
reentrant. No IPv6, EDNS0, DNSSEC or select/poll is implemented.
